      "message": "grep \"height \u003d\u003d 0\" * | wc -l\n267\n\nThe original intent was height \u003d\u003d 0 is not a special case, just a value loop of 0\nThe negative height is a windows GDI capturer convention.\nheight \u003d -height is a silly check for INT_MIN\nin most cases the stride * height-1 multiplied by bpp can overflow and the negative height handling should restrict height to INT_MAX/BPP_MAX\nand the coallesce that does width \u003d width * height; should limit height, but allow a partial coallesce.\nIdeally negative width would also work, but its only easily implemented in rotate and scale.  If it were done after coallesce, a negative width could be done as width \u003d 1, stride \u003d -bpp.\n\nThis \u0027Valid\u0027 is only for most conversions, but a different valid would be needed for scale, rotate and compare.",
